<title>DENMARK: SAS details proposed 1996 dividends.</title>
<headline>SAS details proposed 1996 dividends.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scandinavian Airlines System (SAS) said on Tuesday that its three constituent national companies proposed 1996 dividends of 2.60 Danish crowns, 2.80 Norwegian crowns and 3.00 Swedish crowns.  </p>
<p>The SAS group is jointly owned by the governments of Denmark, Norway and Sweden and private investors through companies in each of the three countries. --Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
